    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1038">

                <pb facs="0873" n="863" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg863"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-24T11:00:00+08:00">March 24, 1949—11
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:56 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>643. Re penultimate paragraph Peiping telegram 440 to Department March 19 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">20</hi>]<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1038-f1"/> which
                    translated CCP<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1038-f2"/> article as explaining Soviet
                    occupation of Dairen and Port Arthur as motivated by intention “to protect them
                    from Japanese aggression”. In English Morse cast [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >English broadcast?</hi>] monitored by Embassy, Soviet occupation Dairen and
                    Port Arthur was explained rather as move to protect them against “imperialist
                    aggression in Far East” which, judging by tenor of article, refers principally
                    to US.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated OffEmb Canton 188, Shanghai 294, Peiping 99.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1038-f1" n="10" xml:id="d1038-f1-content">
